@startuml RAG_Application_Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCE4EC
  BorderColor #C2185B
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  DiamondBorderColor #F57F17
}

title RAG Application Runtime Flow (User Query → Response)

start

:**User Submits Query**
----
* User enters question/request
* Via chat interface, API, or UI
* Capture user context:
  - User ID
  - Session ID
  - Conversation history
  - User preferences
  - Timestamp
* Validate user authentication
* Check rate limits
* Log query initiation;

:**1. Query Reception & Validation**
----
* Receive user query
* Validate input:
  - Check query length
  - Minimum length (e.g., > 3 chars)
  - Maximum length (e.g., < 500 chars)
  - Character encoding
* Check for empty/null queries
* Detect query language
* Sanitize input:
  - Remove malicious content
  - Strip special characters
  - Normalize whitespace
* Assign query ID
* Log query details;

if (Query Valid?) then (No)
  :Return Error Message;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**2. Query Understanding**
----
* Analyze query intent:
  - Factual question
  - How-to request
  - Definition lookup
  - Comparison request
  - Troubleshooting
* Extract key entities:
  - Names, dates, locations
  - Product names
  - Technical terms
* Identify query type
* Detect query complexity
* Classify query category
* Extract filters from query
  (dates, categories, etc.);

:**3. Conversation Context Retrieval**
----
* Fetch conversation history
* Get previous messages
  (last N turns, e.g., 5-10)
* Load user preferences
* Retrieve session state
* Get user metadata
* Load persistent context
* Check for follow-up indicators
  ("it", "that", "also");

:**4. Query Contextualization**
----
* Resolve pronouns/references
  using conversation history
* Merge with conversation context
* Expand implicit information
* Resolve ambiguities
* Create standalone query
  (independent of history)
* Preserve user intent
* Add temporal context;

:**5. Query Preprocessing**
----
* Clean query text:
  - Fix typos/spelling
  - Expand abbreviations
  - Normalize text
  - Handle acronyms
* Remove stop words (optional)
* Apply text normalization
* Tokenize query
* Lemmatization (optional)
* Prepare for embedding;

:**6. Query Expansion (Optional)**
----
* Generate query variations:
  - Synonyms
  - Related terms
  - Alternative phrasings
  - Domain-specific terms
* Create sub-queries
  (for complex questions)
* Add semantic expansions
* Generate hypothetical answers
  (HyDE technique)
* Keep original query weight;

:**7. Query Embedding Generation**
----
* Load embedding model
  (same as indexing model)
* Generate query vector:
  - Convert text to embedding
  - Normalize vector
  - Dimension: e.g., 768, 1536
* Validate embedding quality
* Cache query embedding
  (for repeated queries)
* Handle embedding errors
* Track embedding latency;

:**8. Metadata Filter Construction**
----
* Extract filters from query:
  - Date ranges
  - Categories
  - Document types
  - Sources
  - Tags
* Apply user permissions:
  - Access control
  - Department filters
  - Data sensitivity
* Build filter query
* Combine multiple filters
* Set filter priority;

:**9. Retrieval Configuration**
----
* Set retrieval parameters:
  - Top-K: 5-20 results
  - Similarity threshold: e.g., > 0.7
  - Distance metric: Cosine/Euclidean
* Choose search strategy:
  - Dense vector search
  - Sparse keyword search
  - Hybrid (vector + keyword)
* Configure weights
  (for hybrid search)
* Set diversity parameters
* Apply boost factors;

:**10. Vector Similarity Search**
----
* Query vector database
* Perform similarity calculation:
  - Cosine similarity
  - Dot product
  - Euclidean distance
* Apply metadata filters
* Retrieve top-K candidates:
  - Chunk IDs
  - Similarity scores
  - Chunk text
  - Metadata
* Sort by relevance
* Track search latency
* Handle search errors;

:**11. Initial Results Retrieval**
----
* Fetch chunk text
* Retrieve chunk metadata:
  - Source document
  - Document title
  - Section/page number
  - Timestamp
  - Author
  - URL/file path
* Get similarity scores
* Collect source information
* Validate retrieved chunks
* Check for empty results;

if (Results Found?) then (No)
  :**No Results Handler**
  ----
  * Log failed retrieval
  * Try fallback search:
    - Broader query
    - Reduced filters
    - Keyword search
    - Lower threshold
  * Return graceful message
  * Suggest alternatives
  * Collect feedback;
  
  :Return "No Information Found";
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**12. Reranking (Optional)**
----
* Load reranking model:
  - Cross-encoder model
  - Cohere Rerank API
  - Custom scorer
* Calculate fine-grained relevance:
  - Query-chunk pairs
  - Semantic similarity
  - Contextual relevance
* Compute rerank scores
* Reorder results by score
* Apply score threshold
* Filter low-quality results
* Track reranking time;

:**13. Result Deduplication**
----
* Identify duplicate/similar chunks
* Calculate chunk similarity
* Remove near-duplicates
* Keep highest-scored version
* Preserve diversity:
  - Different sources
  - Different perspectives
  - Different sections
* Maintain source variety;

:**14. Context Assembly**
----
* Select final top-K chunks
  (e.g., top 3-10)
* Order by relevance score
* Format context structure:
  - Add separators
  - Number chunks [1], [2], etc.
  - Add source labels
* Include metadata:
  - Document titles
  - Page/section numbers
  - Timestamps
* Calculate total context length
* Respect LLM context window
  (e.g., 4K, 8K, 32K tokens);

:**15. Context Length Management**
----
* Count context tokens
* Check against LLM limit
* Apply truncation if needed:
  - Remove lower-scored chunks
  - Truncate individual chunks
  - Summarize long chunks
* Prioritize most relevant content
* Preserve context coherence
* Leave room for:
  - System prompt
  - User query
  - Response generation;

:**16. Source Citation Preparation**
----
* Map chunks to sources
* Create citation references:
  - [1] Document A, Page 5
  - [2] Document B, Section 2.3
* Prepare source URLs/links
* Format citations
* Track citation mapping
* Prepare source metadata;

:**17. Prompt Construction**
----
* Load prompt template
* Build structured prompt:
  
  **System Instruction:**
  - Define role and behavior
  - Set answer guidelines
  - Specify citation rules
  
  **Retrieved Context:**
  - Insert formatted chunks
  - Include source citations
  - Number references
  
  **User Query:**
  - Add original query
  - Add any constraints
  
  **Output Instructions:**
  - Response format
  - Citation requirements
  - Length guidelines
* Optimize prompt length
* Validate prompt structure;

:**18. LLM Configuration**
----
* Select LLM model:
  - GPT-4, Claude, Gemini
  - Or self-hosted model
* Set generation parameters:
  - Temperature: 0.0-0.3
    (lower for factual)
  - Max tokens: 500-2000
  - Top-p: 0.9-0.95
  - Frequency penalty: 0.0
  - Presence penalty: 0.0
  - Stop sequences
* Configure streaming (optional)
* Set timeout: e.g., 30s;

:**19. LLM API Call**
----
* Send request to LLM:
  - Prompt with context
  - Configuration parameters
  - API authentication
* Handle streaming response
  (if enabled)
* Monitor token usage:
  - Prompt tokens
  - Completion tokens
  - Total tokens
* Track generation latency
* Handle API errors:
  - Timeout
  - Rate limit
  - Server error
* Implement retry logic;

if (LLM Response\nReceived?) then (No)
  :**Error Handling**
  ----
  * Retry with exponential backoff
  * Try fallback model
  * Return cached response
  * Return error message
  * Log error details;
  
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**20. Response Reception**
----
* Receive LLM response
* Collect full response text
  (or stream chunks)
* Extract token counts
* Record response time
* Validate response received
* Check for completeness
* Handle partial responses;

:**21. Response Parsing**
----
* Extract response text
* Parse citations/references
* Identify inline citations
  [1], [2], etc.
* Extract structured data
  (if requested)
* Parse code blocks
* Parse lists/tables
* Validate response format
* Check for truncation;

:**22. Citation Validation**
----
* Verify citations exist
* Map citations to sources:
  - [1] → Chunk 1 → Document A
  - [2] → Chunk 2 → Document B
* Check citation accuracy
* Validate all citations used
* Identify missing citations
* Cross-reference with context
* Ensure proper attribution;

:**23. Faithfulness Check**
----
* Compare response with context
* Verify claims against sources
* Detect hallucinations:
  - Information not in context
  - Contradictory statements
  - Made-up facts
* Check answer groundedness
* Validate factual accuracy
* Score faithfulness
  (0-1 scale);

if (Faithfulness\nScore > 0.8?) then (No)
  :**Low Faithfulness Handler**
  ----
  * Flag response
  * Add disclaimer
  * Request regeneration
  * Use more conservative prompt
  * Log issue;
  
  note right
    Options:
    - Regenerate
    - Add warning
    - Return with disclaimer
  end note
else (Yes)
endif

:**24. Response Post-Processing**
----
* Format response:
  - Apply markdown
  - Format code blocks
  - Structure paragraphs
  - Add line breaks
* Clean up artifacts
* Apply text polish
* Add section headers (if needed)
* Format lists and tables
* Apply styling;

:**25. Source Link Attachment**
----
* Attach source metadata
* Add clickable source links
* Include document titles
* Add page/section references
* Format source list:
  - "Sources:"
  - [1] Document A - Page 5
  - [2] Document B - Section 2.3
* Add access URLs
* Include timestamps
* Add source previews (optional);

:**26. Confidence Score Calculation**
----
* Calculate overall confidence:
  - Retrieval score
  - Similarity scores
  - Faithfulness score
  - Citation coverage
  - Context quality
* Combine multiple signals
* Normalize score (0-100%)
* Apply thresholds
* Categorize confidence:
  - High (> 80%)
  - Medium (60-80%)
  - Low (< 60%);

:**27. Response Enrichment**
----
* Add metadata:
  - Response time
  - Token usage
  - Number of sources
  - Confidence score
  - Model version
* Add related queries (optional)
* Suggest follow-ups
* Add disclaimers (if needed)
* Include feedback options;

:**28. Content Moderation**
----
* Check response safety:
  - No harmful content
  - No PII leakage
  - No offensive language
  - Appropriate tone
* Apply content policies
* Filter sensitive information
* Validate compliance
* Check legal requirements;

if (Content Safe?) then (No)
  :Block Response;
  :Return Safe Alternative;
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**29. Response Caching**
----
* Generate cache key:
  - Hash of query
  - Context fingerprint
  - Model version
* Store in cache:
  - Response text
  - Sources
  - Metadata
  - TTL: e.g., 1-24 hours
* Update cache statistics
* Manage cache size
* Implement cache invalidation;

:**30. Response Delivery**
----
* Format final response JSON:
  - answer: response text
  - sources: array of sources
  - confidence: score (0-1)
  - metadata: additional info
* Send to user interface
* Support streaming (if enabled)
* Handle delivery errors
* Confirm delivery
* Update response status;

:**User Receives Answer**
----
* Display answer to user
* Show source citations
* Provide source links
* Display confidence (optional)
* Enable follow-up questions
* Show related queries
* Provide feedback options;

:**31. User Interaction Tracking**
----
* Track user actions:
  - Read time
  - Source clicks
  - Copy/share actions
  - Follow-up queries
  - Navigation patterns
* Monitor engagement
* Detect user satisfaction signals
* Track conversion events
* Log interaction data;

:**32. Feedback Collection**
----
* Show feedback options:
  - 👍 Thumbs up
  - 👎 Thumbs down
  - ⭐ Star rating (1-5)
  - 💬 Text feedback
* Collect explicit feedback
* Track implicit feedback:
  - Query reformulation
  - Immediate follow-up
  - Source verification
* Record feedback timestamp
* Associate with query/response;

:**33. Logging & Analytics**
----
* Log complete interaction:
  - Query details
  - Retrieved chunks
  - Response generated
  - Sources used
  - Performance metrics
  - User feedback
* Store for analysis
* Update metrics:
  - Query volume
  - Response time
  - Success rate
  - User satisfaction
* Track costs:
  - Embedding API calls
  - Vector search queries
  - LLM API tokens
* Generate analytics events;

:**34. Performance Metrics**
----
* Calculate metrics:
  - End-to-end latency
  - Retrieval time
  - LLM generation time
  - Token usage
  - Cost per query
  - Cache hit rate
* Compare with SLAs
* Track percentiles (p50, p95, p99)
* Monitor error rates
* Update dashboards;

:**35. Monitoring & Alerts**
----
* Check for anomalies:
  - High latency
  - High error rate
  - Low quality scores
  - Unusual patterns
* Trigger alerts if needed
* Update health metrics
* Track system status
* Monitor resource usage;

:**36. Continuous Learning**
----
* Store query-response pairs
* Collect training data:
  - Good responses (positive feedback)
  - Bad responses (negative feedback)
* Identify improvement areas:
  - Missing information
  - Poor retrievals
  - Hallucinations
* Queue for system optimization
* Update knowledge base
* Refine prompts
* Improve retrieval;

:End of Query Flow;

stop

